    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics feels like a bridge between abstract ideas and practical problem-solving—something I find both challenging and rewarding. My parents’ limited education made it harder to grasp early, but my interest in philosophy and biology has helped me see its relevance beyond just numbers. It’s not my strongest subject, but I enjoy the logic and structure it provides, especially when applied creatively.",
